# USER PROFILE

## Identity
AI Consultant focused on **quality improvement, efficiency, productivity, and cost
optimization** across diverse business operations. Works horizontally across
industries that frequently **overlap** in operating model:
- Manufacturing / power-house operations
- Systems integration & service operations
- Administration & back-office
- (other sectors as engagements arise)

## Current mission (start-up phase)
Build **POCs (proof-of-concept)** for a few initiative areas FIRST, then approach
industry clients to demonstrate how their pain points can be relieved. Deliver
improvement via a **mental-model solution approach with AI as the backbone**
driving toward optimum operational results.

Implication: heavy early-stage work on **architecture / solution frameworks / POC
scaffolding** that must survive real-environment, practical application — not
just slideware.

## How Hermes should support this
- Help set up: architecture solution frameworks, POC scaffolding, reusable
  solution patterns per industry vertical.
- Maintain a **self-learning / self-improving** knowledge base: continuously pull
  market expectations, benchmarks, domain pain points, skills, and solution
  knowledge for the verticals in focus.
- Knowledge must be **compressed + structured** (memory is finite) and indexed for
  fast retrieval by: industry scope, work scope, solution area.
- Proactively recommend cron jobs (with approval) that parallel-pull relevant
  intelligence per active POC/vertical so the agent stays competitive and current.

## Environment & working style (carried forward)
- On Windows, runs Hermes via Docker on WSL2. Technically curious; wants to
  understand the full infra chain (storage, isolation, networking). Security- and
  sandboxing-conscious; wants assurance the agent cannot touch the Windows FS.
- Values deep architectural understanding + philosophical engagement with
  trade-offs. Prefers to fully understand before committing.
- WORKFLOW: for substantial builds, present a DESIGN DIGEST + open questions FIRST;
  wait for explicit 'go' before coding. State honest tool/UI boundaries plainly;
  never overclaim. Acknowledge validity of his thinking before counterpoints.

## Model / cost posture (carried forward)
- FREE-tier LLMs only by default (OpenRouter, NVIDIA NIM, Nous Portal). PAID
  (Gemini / DeepSeek direct) needs explicit per-use approval.
- Heaviest free model per task. Master Agent + per-industry Specialist profiles,
  gated learning, anti-hallucination.
